#
# Counter-example for math:TheoremGroundingShape: a math:Theorem with a declared external
# warrant (so the proof-or-warrant constraint is satisfied) but NO theory context — a bare
# theorem asserted as a truth bit rather than a claim held under a named, versioned theory.
# It fails the sh:minCount on math:roleInTheory, so validation MUST emit
# shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:UngroundedTheoremClaim).
# Bound by ex:ecTheoremMissingTheory.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:untheorizedTheorem a math:Theorem ;
    math:externalWarrant ex:citedPublishedProof .
